# Printing, autowrap and the C0 controls. Cases from Ghostty's VT docs translate their printf scripts as a tty
# delivers them: "\n" arrives as "\r\n" (onlcr), "_" is a blank and "c" the cursor.

=== printing places text at the cursor and moves it right
ref:    ghostty/concepts/cursor.mdx#Cursor
quote:  "The cursor most commonly is associated with where the next printed character will be placed."
size:   10x2
input:  "abc"
screen:
  |abc       |
  |          |
cursor: 3,0

=== printing in the rightmost column sets pending wrap: the cursor stays
ref:    ghostty/concepts/cursor.mdx#Pending Wrap State
quote:  "The pending wrap state is a boolean value that is set when a character is printed in the rightmost column of the screen to indicate that the next printed character should wrap to the next line."
size:   5x2
input:  "abcde"
screen:
  |abcde|
  |     |
cursor: 4,0

=== the next character wraps to the next line
ref:    ghostty/concepts/cursor.mdx#Pending Wrap State
quote:  "If the pending wrap state is set, the next printed character will move the cursor to the leftmost column of the next line, unset the pending wrap state, and then print the character"
size:   5x2
input:  "abcdef"
screen:
  |abcde|
  |f    |
cursor: 1,1

=== backspace after printing in the rightmost column lands left of that character
ref:    ghostty/concepts/cursor.mdx#Pending Wrap State
quote:  "But if you print a character in the rightmost column and then send a [backspace](/docs/vt/control/bs) control character, the cursor will move to the left of the character most recently printed."
size:   5x1
input:  "abcde\bX"
screen:
  |abcXe|
cursor: 4,0

=== backspace elsewhere lands on the character just printed
ref:    ghostty/concepts/cursor.mdx#Pending Wrap State
quote:  "If you print a character in any column other than the rightmost column and then send a [backspace](/docs/vt/control/bs) control character, the cursor will move back on top of the most recently printed character."
size:   5x1
input:  "abc\bX"
screen:
  |abX  |
cursor: 3,0

=== BS is CUB 1 and stops at the left edge
ref:    ghostty/control/bs.mdx#Backspace (BS)
quote:  "This sequence performs [cursor backward (CUB)](/docs/vt/csi/cub) with `Pn = 1`."
size:   5x1
input:  "\b\bX"
screen:
  |X    |
cursor: 1,0

=== CR unsets pending wrap
ref:    ghostty/control/cr.mdx#CR V-1: Pending Wrap is Unset
quote:  "|X________A| |c_________|"
size:   10x2
input:  "\x1b[10GA\rX\r\n"
screen:
  |X        A|
  |          |
cursor: 0,1

=== LF is an index: down a row, same column
ref:    ghostty/control/lf.mdx#Linefeed (LF)
quote:  "This is an alias for [index (IND)](/docs/vt/esc/ind)."
ref:    ghostty/esc/ind.mdx#IND V-1: No Scroll Region, Top of Screen
quote:  "|A_________| |_Xc_______|"
size:   10x2
input:  "A\nX"
screen:
  |A         |
  | X        |
cursor: 2,1

=== LF at the bottom scrolls the screen into the scrollback
ref:    ghostty/esc/ind.mdx#Index (IND)
quote:  "If the scroll region is the full terminal screen and the terminal is on the [primary screen](#TODO), this may create scrollback."
size:   5x2
input:  "one\r\ntwo\r\nthree\r\nfour"
screen:
  |three|
  |four |
history:
  one
  two
cursor: 4,1

=== HT moves to the next tab stop
ref:    ghostty/control/tab.mdx#Tab (TAB)
quote:  "This is an alias for [cursor horizontal tabulation (CHT)](/docs/vt/csi/cht) with `n = 1`."
ref:    ghostty/csi/cht.mdx#CHT V-2: Right From Before a Tabstop
quote:  "|_A______X_|"
size:   10x1
input:  "\x1b[?5W\x1b[1;2HA\tX"
screen:
  | A      X |
cursor: 9,0

=== HT stops at the last column
ref:    ghostty/csi/cht.mdx#CHT V-1: Right Beyond Last Column
quote:  "|_________A|"
size:   10x1
input:  "\x1b[?5W\x1b[100IA"
screen:
  |         A|
cursor: 9,0

=== tab stops default to every 8 columns
ref:    xterm/ctlseqs.txt CSI ? 5 W
quote:  "Reset tab stops to start with column 9, every 8 columns (DECST8C), VT510."
size:   20x1
input:  "a\tb\tc"
screen:
  |a       b       c   |
cursor: 17,0
